A IN SITU  3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the posterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  6  TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  14  Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   3  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   3  Extracapsular extension  Marked  Other forms of axillary involvement  Lymphatic vessels  There is granulation tissue and fibrosis present in lymph nodes involved with tumor  The presence of isolated tumor cells in some lymph nodes  may reflect regression from a larger focus of metastatic carcinoma following neoadjuvant therapy  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Meagher  REMOVE_MRN and  left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue  with a localization wire in place  A short black stitch designates the superior margin  and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm gray white stellate scar with central hemorrhage and an eccentric 0 8cm cavity  consistent with a previous biopsy site  The cavity comes to 0 2cm of the anterior margin  0 8cm of the superior margin  1 1cm of the posterior margin  2 0cm of the inferior margin  2 3cm of the medial margin  and 2 0cm of the lateral margin  The gray white stellate fibrous area comes to 0 3cm of the posterior margin  0 7cm of the of the superior margin  0 8cm of the anterior margin  1 5cm of the inferior margin  1 3cm of the medial margin  and 1 6cm of the lateral margin  A single silv