r protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is an oriented mastectomy specimen  with a suture designating the superior aspect  The deep resection margin is inked black and the superior resection margin is inked blue  The mastectomy is overlaid by REMOVED_DATE x 14 0cm ellipse of white pink skin  On its lateral aspect is a longitudinal 7 0cm long  well healed linear scar Sectioning through the breast parenchyma reveals at least two stellate irregular  firm nodular areas  located slightly superior to the nipple  The more lateral measures 3 0cm in greatest dimension and REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in cross section  It is white  firm stellate with central spiculation and located approximately 1 5cm from the closest  deep  resection margin  The second area is slightly more medial to the nipple and measures 3 4cm in greatest dimension  REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm in cross section  This area has more nodular lobular appearance and is within 0 5cm of the closest  deep  resection margin  This second nodule has a central area of red hemorrhage    previous site of fine needle aspiration   In the axillary node region is a large firm lymph node 7 0cm in greatest diameter completely replaced by tumor with gray white lobulation  Section code  A  Lateral nodule B C  Resection margin closest to lateral nodule D E  Medial nodule in relation to resection margin F  More medial nodule  area suspicious for biopsy site G H  Large axillary node  represnetative sections I J  Lymph nodes K M  Query lymph nodes Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Yes.
